# Windvale Community Source License 1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 E-Worker Inc and Windvale contributors

## 1. Purpose and status

These terms make the source code available for personal, educational,
research, evaluation, and qualifying small-organization use, while reserving
large-organization production use and direct commercial exploitation for a
separate commercial agreement.

This is a source-available license. It is not an Open Source Initiative
approved open-source license.

## 2. Definitions

**Affiliate** means an entity that directly or indirectly controls, is
controlled by, or is under common control with another entity. **Control**
means ownership of more than fifty percent of the voting interests or the
power to direct the entity's management and policies.

**Commercial Threshold** means total consolidated gross revenue of more than
20,000,000 United States dollars during the immediately preceding consecutive
twelve-month period. Revenue of You and all Your Affiliates is aggregated and
measured consistently with the accounting standards used for Your
consolidated financial reporting. Revenue reported in another currency is
converted using a reasonable published central-bank average exchange rate for
the relevant period.

**Covered Software** means the Windvale source code, object code,
documentation, specifications, tools, and other material to which the
Licensor expressly applies these terms. It does not include third-party
material identified as being under another license.

**Distribute** means to provide a copy of the Covered Software or a Derivative
Work to another person or entity by any means.

**Evaluation Use** means non-production use solely to inspect, test, perform
security analysis on, or determine whether to adopt or purchase rights in the
Covered Software. Evaluation Use does not include using the Covered Software
to operate a live system, provide a product or service, perform ordinary
organizational work, or create production deliverables.

**Licensor** means E-Worker Inc and each other copyright holder that expressly
offers its contribution under these terms.

**Noncommercial Use** means use that is not primarily intended for commercial
advantage or monetary compensation. Personal learning, public education,
independent research, and charitable activity are examples, provided that the
use is not performed for the commercial benefit of another organization. Use
by a for-profit organization for its operations, personnel, products,
services, customers, or strategic benefit is not Noncommercial Use.

**Production Use** means use of the Covered Software in a live system or to
develop, build, operate, secure, support, or deliver an organization's normal
operations, products, or services. Production Use includes internal use by an
organization and does not require that third parties receive access to the
Covered Software.

**Qualifying Small Organization** means You and Your Affiliates collectively
do not exceed the Commercial Threshold at the time of use.

**Corresponding Source** means the preferred form for making modifications,
including source code, documentation source, and the scripts and configuration
reasonably necessary to build the corresponding object code, but excluding
generally available tools and unmodified third-party dependencies.

**Windvale-as-a-Product Use** means using the Covered Software or a Derivative
Work as the principal basis of a commercial operating system, runtime,
compiler or developer-tool distribution, hosted or managed execution service,
hardware or software appliance, original-equipment-manufacturer offering, or
other product whose principal commercial value is providing Windvale itself
or substantially equivalent capabilities.

**You** means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under these
terms.

A **Derivative Work** has the meaning given by applicable copyright law.

## 3. Permitted uses

By exercising any permission granted under these terms, You accept these terms
as conditions of Your license. Subject to these terms, the Licensor grants You
a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable copyright license
to use, reproduce, modify, and Distribute the Covered Software only for the
following purposes:

1. Noncommercial Use;
2. Evaluation Use;
3. personal use by a natural person acting on their own behalf and not for an
   employer, client, or other organization; or
4. Production Use by a Qualifying Small Organization, except for
   Windvale-as-a-Product Use.

You may exercise more than one permitted purpose. No purpose outside this
section is licensed by these terms.

Use by a contractor, service provider, distributor, or other agent on behalf
of another person or organization is treated as use by both parties. Each must
independently qualify for the use under these terms or a separate commercial
agreement.

## 4. Uses requiring a commercial agreement

You must obtain a separate written commercial agreement from E-Worker Inc or
the applicable Licensor before:

1. engaging in Production Use when You and Your Affiliates exceed the
   Commercial Threshold;
2. engaging in Windvale-as-a-Product Use, regardless of revenue;
3. offering third parties access for compensation or commercial advantage to
   the Covered Software's compiler, runtime, operating-system, execution,
   build, security, or development capabilities as a hosted or managed
   service; or
4. Distributing the Covered Software or a Derivative Work under proprietary
   terms or without satisfying Section 6.

Commercial terms may include support, security maintenance, certification,
indemnity, original-equipment-manufacturer rights, proprietary distribution,
trademark rights, or other negotiated rights. These terms do not require a
Licensor to offer or enter into a commercial agreement.

## 5. Crossing the Commercial Threshold

A Qualifying Small Organization that later exceeds the Commercial Threshold
may continue its existing Production Use for ninety days after the end of the
month in which it first exceeds the threshold. Before that period ends, it
must obtain a commercial agreement or discontinue all use that is not
otherwise permitted by Section 3.

Corporate restructuring, use through an Affiliate, or allocation of revenue
among related entities does not avoid the Commercial Threshold.

## 6. Distribution and source availability

If You Distribute the Covered Software or a Derivative Work under these terms,
You must:

1. provide each recipient with a copy of these terms and all copyright,
   attribution, patent, and license notices included with the Covered
   Software;
2. identify files You materially modified and state the date of modification;
3. provide the Corresponding Source with the distribution or make it
   available without charge through a durable, publicly accessible location
   for at least three years after the distribution; and
4. license the Covered Software and Your modifications to it under these same
   terms, without imposing additional restrictions on the exercise of rights
   granted here.

Each recipient receives rights in the Covered Software directly from the
applicable Licensors by accepting these terms. You may not sublicense the
Covered Software or represent that a recipient receives broader rights under
these terms than You do.

These requirements apply only to the Covered Software and Derivative Works.

## 7. Independent applications and runtime exception

Subject to Your right to use the Covered Software under Section 3 or a
separate commercial agreement, You choose the license and other terms for an
independent application, service, content item, data set, or other work that
You create (an **Application**). The Licensors claim no ownership of an
Application merely because it:

1. is written in the Windvale language;
2. is compiled, assembled, linked, packaged, tested, or otherwise processed
   by the Covered Software;
3. uses documented Windvale APIs, ABIs, system calls, bytecode, module, object,
   package, or executable formats;
4. communicates with the Covered Software through a documented interface; or
5. contains generated output that does not itself reproduce a substantial
   portion of the Covered Software.

**Redistributable Runtime Material** means portions of the Covered Software
that official Windvale tools automatically or ordinarily copy, link, or embed
in an Application so that the Application can start or run, including startup
code and runtime or library components expressly identified as
redistributable.

You may reproduce, link, embed, and Distribute unmodified Redistributable
Runtime Material solely as part of an Application. You may license the
Application under terms of Your choice. Inclusion of Redistributable Runtime
Material does not extend these terms to the Application as a whole or give a
Licensor rights in the Application.

Redistributable Runtime Material remains Covered Software. You must retain its
copyright and license notices and provide recipients with a copy of these
terms. If You modify Redistributable Runtime Material, Section 6 applies to
those modifications, but its source-availability requirements do not extend
to the independent portions of the Application.

This exception does not permit You to extract or Distribute the Covered
Software as a standalone product, to make a derivative or replacement of a
Windvale compiler, runtime, operating system, library, or tool, or to engage
in Windvale-as-a-Product Use without the required commercial agreement.

